  abstract = {Digital technologies enable new teaching and learning formats in hybrid or purely virtual forms. The project “DigiFit4All” aims to create Personalised Open Online Courses (POOCs) in computer science and digital education based on competency models and learner testing. One challenge is the broad scope of the project, since at least the following four target groups are considered: pupils, students, teachers and administrative staff. For each target group, a specific competency model will be selected to form the basis for developing digital learning materials. This paper describes the target groups, the content selection process and the individual models.},
