  urldate = {2025-07-27},
  abstract = {What assumptions about learning, knowledge and participation are behind terms such as recommendation system, sequencing rule, filtering, adaptive learning path or AI use scenario? What societal and ethical discussions open up through the use of generative AI and an associated "algorithmic bias"? In this glossary, the author takes a critical look at terms and concepts in the context of AI in education. She provides an orientation to a developing terminology that constantly creates neologisms. The selection of the terms described in the article comes from Issue 55 of The Austrian Open Access Journal on Adult Education (meb). The author structures her glossary into eight categories: basic AI terms, technological fundamentals, systems and infrastructure, recommendation systems and AI logic, law and technology, education-related AI terms, society and ethics and AI-assisted didactics and learning processes. (DIPF/Orig.)},
